{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/category_card

    One course of the category showcase. The same markup serves the card view
    and the dense list view - the view is one class on the listing container,
    never a second template - and the panel's rail restyles it as a mini card.

    Anatomy: a media band holding the course image (or the flat fallback the
    stylesheet paints), the event's date tile and the kind pill; a body with the
    subcategory overline, the title and its link, the meta line (opened, for a
    course tool_courserating rates and somebody rated, by its rating: an amber
    glyph, the average and the count, all hidden from a screen reader, which is
    told the rating's sentence instead; a rating with no other fact still draws
    the line), then the badge
    row - the course's crests, the state pill (the design system's own pair of
    tokens, never a Bootstrap utility, with a decorative icon before its
    sentence) and, for staff, the hidden badge; then the route line, only on a
    card whose viewer holds a row that is not active and could also enrol now
    (the sentence beside the call to action
    that goes there); in the same place, the opening line, only on a card whose
    way in is refused until an enrolment window opens, with that date (plain
    text, its icon decorative); then the trailing action cluster - the call to action, the "More information"
    link, and last the favourite star, so that in
    list view it falls into the cluster's flow beside the button instead of over
    the kind glyph. The star is drawn only for a logged-in viewer and stays
    hidden until a client module marks the body (the star's dim-star-js, or
    the listing's dim-js), because a star that does nothing is worse than none.

    Every text value arrives in the plain spelling and is escaped here.

    The article also carries the facts the filter line's preview decides a
    criterion on (js/esm/src/filterline/preview.ts): data-chip, the state chip the course counts
    under (empty on a visitor's card); data-fields, the filter fields the card
    may state as fieldid:value pairs, 0 for no value, a field the card may not
    state left out; and data-start, the start day in the site's timezone, empty
    for a course with none and absent where the card may not state it. The
    favourite is the star's own aria-pressed. category_card decides each.

    The client modules address this template through data attributes only,
    never a class: a class is presentation and moves with the design, and a
    renamed hook reddens the markup test instead of silently disarming a
    behaviour. The article (dim-card) carries the course id and the classifier
    state, which is how the modules know which cards to ask progress for;
    dim-card-more is the "More information" link, dim-card-cover the cover and
    dim-card-pill the state pill, which the course dialogue copies;
    dim-card-titlelink takes the focus on the first appended card when no load-more button or next-page
    link remains; dim-card-title, the heading rather than the link, is where the
    search term is marked, because a visitor's card with no page to open draws
    its title as plain text; the badge row holds an empty, hidden
    dim-card-progress span the module fills with the progress sentence, so no
    row changes height when a batch lands; and the star carries both spellings
    of its label plus a hook on the visually hidden span, so pressing it
    relabels it without a round trip.

    The crests are written in the badge row and not in the media band, although
    the card view draws them over it: the list view puts them in the right-hand
    cluster beside the state badge, and one markup serves both views. The
    stylesheet lifts them onto the image with an absolute position, as it does
    the star. They are the course's own badges - the ones its enrolment page
    shows - and never the category's.

    dim-card__badge, beside each badge's own classes, is the card's hook on its
    badges: the panel's rail resizes them through it, while the design-system
    classes keep every colour.

    Its cover is lazy unless the listing puts the card in the first row of the
    page's first paint (eager), and the first such cover is fetched ahead of
    every other image (priority) only where the hero paints no picture.

    "More information" is a link to the card's own page (url: the course, the
    landing page or the enrolment page), drawn only where the card has one;
    without JavaScript it leads there, where everything about the course is.
    For an account, categorycoursemodal intercepts it and opens the course
    dialogue at once from what the card holds - the cover, the pill, the title,
    and the page's decision written onto the link from modal: the kicker
    (data-kicker), the primary button (data-primary with its icon, and either
    data-primary-url or, for an enrolment that opens later, data-primary-closed
    carrying what a screen reader is told) and the secondary one (data-secondary,
    data-secondary-url) - then fills it with the content it fetches.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "id": 42,
        "fullname": "Pre-hospital Care & Rescue",
        "url": "https://example.com/enrol/index.php?id=42",
        "hasurl": true,
        "overline": "Brigade",
        "hasoverline": true,
        "imageurl": "https://example.com/pluginfile.php/31/course/overviewfiles/capa.jpg",
        "hasimage": true,
        "eager": false,
        "priority": false,
        "badges": [
            {"url": "https://example.com/pluginfile.php/31/theme_dimensions/badge/42/abc/crest-alpha.png", "alt": "crest alpha"},
            {"url": "https://example.com/pluginfile.php/31/theme_dimensions/badge/42/def/dimensions.svg", "alt": "dimensions"}
        ],
        "hasbadges": true,
        "badgeslabel": "Institutions",
        "isevent": false,
        "kindlabel": "Course",
        "haskind": true,
        "datetile": {"day": "12", "month": "Nov"},
        "meta": "36 hours · In-person · São Paulo",
        "rating": {"avg": "4.7", "count": 23, "label": "Rating 4.7 out of 5, 23 ratings"},
        "hasrating": true,
        "state": "scheduled",
        "chip": "scheduled",
        "fieldvalues": "12:1 14:0",
        "hasstartday": true,
        "startday": "2026-11-12",
        "badge": {"label": "Access from 12 Nov 2026", "classes": "dim-badge dim-badge--scheduled", "icon": "fa-calendar"},
        "hasroute": true,
        "routelabel": "You can also enrol now",
        "hasopens": false,
        "openslabel": "",
        "ishidden": false,
        "hiddenbadge": {"label": "Hidden from students", "classes": "dim-badge dim-badge--hidden"},
        "ismuted": false,
        "cta": {"label": "Enrol now", "url": "https://example.com/enrol/index.php?id=42", "primary": false},
        "showstar": true,
        "favourite": false,
        "starlabel": "Add to favourites: Pre-hospital Care & Rescue",
        "starlabeladd": "Add to favourites: Pre-hospital Care & Rescue",
        "starlabelremove": "Remove from favourites: Pre-hospital Care & Rescue",
        "detailslabel": "More information",
        "modal": {
            "kicker": "Brigade",
            "haskicker": true,
            "primary": {"label": "Enrol now", "url": "https://example.com/enrol/index.php?id=42", "disabled": false, "note": "", "icon": "fa-arrow-right"},
            "secondary": {"label": "Course page", "url": "https://example.com/theme/dimensions/landing.php?id=42"}
        }
    }
}}
<article class="dim-card{{#ismuted}} dim-card--muted{{/ismuted}}" data-region="dim-card" data-courseid="{{id}}" data-state="{{state}}" data-chip="{{chip}}" data-fields="{{fieldvalues}}"{{#hasstartday}} data-start="{{startday}}"{{/hasstartday}}>
    <div class="dim-card__media{{#hasimage}} dim-card__media--image{{/hasimage}}">
        {{#hasimage}}
        <img class="dim-card__image" data-region="dim-card-cover" src="{{imageurl}}" alt=""{{^eager}} loading="lazy"{{/eager}}{{#priority}} fetchpriority="high"{{/priority}} decoding="async" width="320" height="150">
        {{/hasimage}}
        {{#datetile}}
        <span class="dim-card__datetile"><b>{{day}}</b><span>{{month}}</span></span>
        {{/datetile}}
        {{#haskind}}
        <span class="dim-card__kind{{#isevent}} dim-card__kind--event{{/isevent}}"><i class="fa {{#isevent}}fa-calendar-day{{/isevent}}{{^isevent}}fa-graduation-cap{{/isevent}}" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="dim-card__kindlabel">{{kindlabel}}</span></span>
        {{/haskind}}
    </div>
    <div class="dim-card__body">
        <div class="dim-card__titlewrap">
            {{#hasoverline}}
            <span class="dim-card__over">{{overline}}</span>
            {{/hasoverline}}
            <h3 class="dim-card__title" data-region="dim-card-title">{{#hasurl}}<a href="{{url}}" title="{{fullname}}" data-region="dim-card-titlelink">{{fullname}}</a>{{/hasurl}}{{^hasurl}}<span title="{{fullname}}">{{fullname}}</span>{{/hasurl}}</h3>
            {{#hasrating}}
            <p class="dim-card__meta"><span class="dim-card__rating"><span aria-hidden="true"><i class="fa fa-star dim-card__ratingstar" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{rating.avg}} ({{rating.count}})</span><span class="visually-hidden">{{rating.label}}</span></span>{{#meta}} · {{meta}}{{/meta}}</p>
            {{/hasrating}}
            {{^hasrating}}
            {{#meta}}
            <p class="dim-card__meta">{{meta}}</p>
            {{/meta}}
            {{/hasrating}}
        </div>
        <div class="dim-card__row">
            {{#hasbadges}}
            <ul class="dim-card__crests" role="list" aria-label="{{badgeslabel}}">
                {{#badges}}
                <li class="dim-card__crest"><img src="{{url}}" alt="{{alt}}" width="80" height="88" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></li>
                {{/badges}}
            </ul>
            {{/hasbadges}}
            <span class="dim-card__badge {{badge.classes}}" data-region="dim-card-pill"><i class="fa {{badge.icon}}" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{badge.label}}</span>
            {{#ishidden}}
            <span class="dim-card__badge {{hiddenbadge.classes}}"><i class="fa fa-eye-slash" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{hiddenbadge.label}}</span>
            {{/ishidden}}
            <span class="dim-card__prog" data-region="dim-card-progress" hidden></span>
        </div>
        {{#hasroute}}
        <p class="dim-card__route"><i class="fa fa-arrow-right" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{routelabel}}</p>
        {{/hasroute}}
        {{#hasopens}}
        <p class="dim-card__opens"><i class="fa fa-calendar-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i> {{openslabel}}</p>
        {{/hasopens}}
        <div class="dim-card__actions">
            {{#cta}}
            <a class="btn btn-sm dim-card__cta {{#primary}}btn-primary{{/primary}}{{^primary}}btn-outline-primary{{/primary}}" href="{{url}}">{{label}}</a>
            {{/cta}}
            {{#hasurl}}
            <a class="btn btn-sm dim-card__summary" href="{{url}}" data-region="dim-card-more"{{#modal}}{{#haskicker}} data-kicker="{{kicker}}"{{/haskicker}}{{#primary}} data-primary="{{label}}" data-primary-icon="{{icon}}"{{#disabled}} data-primary-closed="{{note}}"{{/disabled}}{{^disabled}} data-primary-url="{{url}}"{{/disabled}}{{/primary}}{{#secondary}} data-secondary="{{label}}" data-secondary-url="{{url}}"{{/secondary}}{{/modal}}>{{detailslabel}}</a>
            {{/hasurl}}
            {{#showstar}}
            <button type="button" class="dim-card__star dim-js-only" aria-pressed="{{#favourite}}true{{/favourite}}{{^favourite}}false{{/favourite}}" data-action="dim-star" data-courseid="{{id}}" data-star-add="{{starlabeladd}}" data-star-remove="{{starlabelremove}}"><i class="{{#favourite}}fa-solid{{/favourite}}{{^favourite}}fa-regular{{/favourite}} fa-star" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="visually-hidden" data-region="dim-star-label">{{starlabel}}</span></button>
            {{/showstar}}
        </div>
    </div>
</article>
